## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: `Game` class holds all state; `mulberry32` seeded RNG (`this.rng()`) used for events, colonist gen, storms; `endTurn()` calls fireEvent→produceResources→consumeResources→updateMorale→ashstorm in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `generateMap()` builds 64 tiles from seed formula; `buildBuilding()` checks `b.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `getAdjacencyBonus()` feeds `adjBonus` into forge/greenhouse/condenser yield formulas. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: ore→metal (mine→forge), ash→soil→food (soilMaker→greenhouse) chains consume inputs; `Math.min(this.state.caps.x, ...)` caps every output. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job/assignedBuilding; `avgSkill` and `fatigueModifier` read in `produceResources()` directly drive yield. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `consumeResources()` deducts food/water, drops morale on shortage, `updateMorale()` recovers morale over time — but morale is never read in `produceResources()`, so "morale changes output" link is missing. Score 1.

**F6 Research**: 8 nodes, prereq gating via `state.research[k].available`, costs deducted in `research()`; unlocks work and construction/shielding/medicine apply real effects, but hydroponics ("+30% water") and efficiency ("+20% production") are never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 Events**: 10 events defined; weighted selection via `totalWeight`/`r` loop; 4 events (morale_crisis, merchant, sickness, pests) have differentiated choice effects; `firedEvents[id]` gives 10-turn cooldown. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `caravanPrices` set once in `initPrices()` and never updated (no drift, `globalDemand` unused); buy/sell both work via `trade()`. Score 1.

**F9 Hazard**: `ashstorm()` scales severity with turn, damages `b.health`, reduced by construction/shielding research — but `produceResources()` never reads building health, and no "repair" function exists anywhere. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load**: `serialize()` dumps full state to textarea; `deserialize()` try/catches JSON.parse and shows error via `loadMsg`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water>=100`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`) both reachable; only "WIN"/"GAME OVER" text shown, no computed score from multiple state values. Score 1.

**F12 UI**: `switchTab()` wires tabs/panels; log entries show `T{turn}`; tooltips show building/terrain info; Space/1-6 keyboard shortcuts; `@media (max-width:600px)` responsive CSS. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts real invariants (caps, skill/morale/fatigue ranges, prereqs, save/load hash match); `runBench()` runs 200 turns headlessly on a separate `Game` instance and prints `hash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `BUILDINGS[bld].unlocked=true` set in `research()`; `buildBuilding()` gates construction on `unlocked`/research done — but `produceResources()` itself never reads any research flag, so yield formulas don't scale with research (hydroponics/efficiency bonuses unused). Score 2.

**G2**: `consumeResources()` writes morale drop on shortage (real state change) but `produceResources()` never reads `c.morale`; only path back to output is colonists leaving at morale=0 in `updateMorale()`, an indirect special case. Score 2.

**G3**: `ashstorm()` damages `b.health`, but `produceResources()` never checks building health, and no repair function exists anywhere in the file — chain breaks after damage. Score 1.

**G4**: `caravanPrices` fixed at init, never modified by stockpiles or turns; `globalDemand` declared but unread. Score 0.

**G5**: `makeChoice(i)` calls `evt.choices[i].effect(game)` for morale_crisis/merchant/sickness/pests, each writing distinct resource/morale/state changes, not just log text. Score 4.

